<<<
+ of understand(ing), the ap- forms denote the getting hold or grasping, & the com- forms the having hold or full ession, of what is understood.
===
+ of *understand(ing)*, the *ap-* forms denote the getting hold or grasping, & the *com-* forms the having hold or full possession, of what is understood.
>>>

<<<
What is beyond my apprehension I have no cognizance of; what is beyond my comprehension I am merely incapable of fully understanding.
===
What is *beyond my apprehension* I have no cognizance of; what is *beyond my comprehension* I am merely incapable of fully understanding.
>>>

<<<
To apprehend a thing imperfectly is to have not reached a clear notion of it; to comprehend it imperfectly is almost a contradiction in terms.
===
To *apprehend* a thing *imperfectly* is to have not reached a clear notion of it; to *comprehend* it *imperfectly* is almost a contradiction in terms.
>>>

<<<
J apprehend that A is B advances an admittedly fallible view; I comprehend that A is B states a presumably indisputable fact.
===
*I apprehend that A is* B advances an admittedly fallible view; *I comprehend that A is* B states a presumably indisputable fact.
>>>

